  "summary": "Grammars whose productions rewrite a single nonterminal, introduced by Chomsky (1956) and, as BNF, used to define ALGOL 60. They generate exactly the languages of pushdown automata and are the basis of programming-language syntax definitions and parsing algorithms (LL, LR, Earley, CYK).",
